  data: {
    LLM: '1. After cards are on foreheads, a round of betting occurs (ante, then betting as agreedâ€”limit, pot-limit, or no-limit). 2. Players act in turn: fold, check, call, or raise. 3. Showdown: all remaining players reveal. Highest card wins. Ties split the pot. 4. Optional: play lowest wins, or high-low split.',
    Player: '1. After cards are on foreheads, a round of betting occurs (ante, then betting as agreedâ€”limit, pot-limit, or no-limit). 2. Players act in turn: fold, check, call, or raise. 3. Showdown: all remaining players reveal. Highest card wins. Ties split the pot. 4. Optional: play lowest wins, or high-low split.',
    objective: 'Win the pot by holding the highest card among those who did not fold, or by making all others fold.',
    gameplay: '1. After cards are on foreheads, a round of betting occurs (ante, then betting as agreedâ€”limit, pot-limit, or no-limit). 2. Players act in turn: fold, check, call, or raise. 3. Showdown: all remaining players reveal. Highest card wins. Ties split the pot. 4. Optional: play lowest wins, or high-low split.',
    keyRules: [
      "Each player sees all other players' cards but not their own.",
      'Ace is high; no suit order for tie-breakingâ€”tied cards split.',
      'Match-pot variant: players declare stay or drop (simultaneously or in turn); best card of those who stayed wins; others who stayed must match the pot.',
      'With simultaneous declaration, two high-card holders can both drop seeing each other; savvy players may exploit this.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: "Two to eight players. The one-card variant is the basic form: each player is dealt one card face down, picks it up without looking, and holds it against the forehead so all others can see its value. A round of betting follows; at showdown the highest card among those who did not fold wins the pot. The game is usually played with 2–8; skills involved are probability and reading other players' actions and bets.",
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck. Ace high; no suit ranking for ties.',
      equipment: 'Standard deck, poker chips.',
      dealing: 'Each player antes. Dealer deals one card face-down to each player. Players pick up their card without looking, hold it facing outward, and place it against their forehead so all others can see it.',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. After cards are on foreheads, a round of betting occurs (ante, then betting as agreedâ€”limit, pot-limit, or no-limit). 2. Players act in turn: fold, check, call, or raise. 3. Showdown: all remaining players reveal. Highest card wins. Ties split the pot. 4. Optional: play lowest wins, or high-low split.',
